    "Notes": "The engine's own look, stated as tokens. Every colour here is the value the matching component field defaults to, digit for digit, so a canvas that switches from no theme to this one renders the frame it rendered before \u2014 which is what makes it usable as the control half of a theme A/B. The HighContrastColors table is deliberately short: it holds only the tokens whose foreground/background separation is too low, and every token without a row here keeps its ordinary value.",
